And there is one detail in his story that

17
00:00:41,140 --> 00:00:42,884
still has not been explained.

18
00:00:42,904 --> 00:00:46,060
According to a court filing reported by Mexican journalists,

19
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:49,235
he may have already stood before a judge in

20
00:00:49,255 --> 00:00:52,058
San Diego, a year and a half earlier.

21
00:00:54,798 --> 00:00:57,559
Chapter 1. The other Chapo.

22
00:01:02,159 --> 00:01:05,878
First, the name. He is not Joaquín Guzmán,

23
00:01:05,898 --> 00:01:07,747
the famous El Chapo,

24
00:01:07,767 --> 00:01:11,018
now serving life in an American supermax.

25
00:01:11,038 --> 00:01:15,224
Chapo is a common Mexican nickname for a short,

26
00:01:15,244 --> 00:01:18,495
stocky man. This is a different Chapo.

27
00:01:20,415 --> 00:01:22,307
According to Mexican sources,

28
00:01:22,327 --> 00:01:26,608
Fausto Isidro Meza Flores was born in June nineteen

29
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:28,519
eighty two, in Bamoa,

30
00:01:28,539 --> 00:01:30,908
in the municipality of Guasave,

31
00:01:30,928 --> 00:01:33,298
in the state of Sinaloa.

32
00:01:33,318 --> 00:01:37,121
Other sources place his birth in neighboring Sonora.

33
00:01:38,441 --> 00:01:41,686
Sinaloa is the cradle of Mexican drug trafficking.

34
00:01:41,706 --> 00:01:44,543
It gave the world the Sinaloa Cartel,

35
00:01:44,563 --> 00:01:47,808
and many of the men who built it.

36
00:01:49,128 --> 00:01:50,833
According to published accounts,

37
00:01:50,853 --> 00:01:52,557
Meza Flores started young,

38
00:01:52,577 --> 00:01:54,281
in the nineteen nineties,

39
00:01:54,301 --> 00:01:56,436
working for the Juárez Cartel.

40
00:01:56,456 --> 00:02:00,316
Then he moved to the organization of the Beltrán

41
00:02:00,336 --> 00:02:04,195
Leyva brothers. One account describes him as the right

42
00:02:04,215 --> 00:02:06,781
hand man of Héctor Beltrán Leyva.

43
00:02:08,321 --> 00:02:10,932
Chapter 2. The split.

44
00:02:15,532 --> 00:02:19,449
The Beltrán Leyva brothers had once been part of

45
00:02:19,469 --> 00:02:22,511
the Sinaloa alliance. Around two thousand eight,

46
00:02:22,531 --> 00:02:25,573
they broke away, and a war began.

47
00:02:26,893 --> 00:02:29,304
In December two thousand nine,

48
00:02:29,324 --> 00:02:32,221
Mexican marines killed the eldest brother,

49
00:02:32,241 --> 00:02:36,596
Arturo Beltrán Leyva, in a shootout in the city

50
00:02:36,616 --> 00:02:39,999
of Cuernavaca. His organization started to fracture.

51
00:02:41,319 --> 00:02:44,494
Some of his men went their own way.

52
00:02:44,514 --> 00:02:46,891
Meza Flores, according to these accounts,

53
00:02:46,911 --> 00:02:49,287
stayed loyal to the remaining brothers.

54
00:02:49,307 --> 00:02:52,482
And slowly, he built something of his own.

55
00:02:54,602 --> 00:02:58,088
His group became known as Los Mazatlecos,

56
00:02:58,108 --> 00:03:00,092
or the Guasave Cartel.

57
00:03:00,112 --> 00:03:02,095
According to Mexican sources,

58
00:03:02,115 --> 00:03:05,101
its territory stretched across northern Sinaloa,

59
00:03:05,121 --> 00:03:07,605
into the state of Nayarit,

60
00:03:07,625 --> 00:03:10,611
and as far as Los Cabos.

61
00:03:11,931 --> 00:03:14,271
In April two thousand ten,

62
00:03:14,291 --> 00:03:16,159
soldiers almost caught him,

63
00:03:16,179 --> 00:03:19,936
in the mountains of Choix in northern Sinaloa.

64
00:03:19,956 --> 00:03:24,185
According to reports, two soldiers and twelve gunmen were

65
00:03:24,205 --> 00:03:25,601
killed. He escaped.

66
00:03:27,721 --> 00:03:30,171
That summer, in July twenty ten,

67
00:03:30,191 --> 00:03:33,875
a battle broke out near the town of Tubutama

68
00:03:33,895 --> 00:03:36,344
in Sonora, close to the U.S.

69
00:03:36,364 --> 00:03:39,637
border, between Sinaloa Cartel gunmen and their rivals.

70
00:03:39,657 --> 00:03:41,283
According to published accounts,

71
00:03:41,303 --> 00:03:44,987
Meza Flores was one of the men who led

72
00:03:45,007 --> 00:03:48,691
the ambush. Reports of the death toll range from

73
00:03:48,711 --> 00:03:50,749
twenty one to around thirty.

74
00:03:52,069 --> 00:03:54,257
His patrons did not last.

75
00:03:54,277 --> 00:03:57,790
Héctor Beltrán Leyva was arrested in twenty fourteen,

76
00:03:57,810 --> 00:04:01,764
and died of a heart attack in custody in

77
00:04:01,784 --> 00:04:03,530
twenty eighteen. By then,

78
00:04:03,550 --> 00:04:07,063
the man from Guasave no longer needed them.

79
00:04:08,603 --> 00:04:10,889
Chapter 3. Wanted.

80
00:04:15,489 --> 00:04:19,134
The United States had been watching him for years.

81
00:04:19,154 --> 00:04:20,762
According to Mexican media,

82
00:04:20,782 --> 00:04:24,427
he was first indicted in Washington in twenty twelve.

83
00:04:25,747 --> 00:04:27,567
In January twenty thirteen,

84
00:04:27,587 --> 00:04:31,707
the U.S. Treasury sanctioned him under the Kingpin Act,

85
00:04:31,727 --> 00:04:33,547
along with his father,

86
00:04:33,567 --> 00:04:35,387
his mother, his wife,

87
00:04:35,407 --> 00:04:38,607
his sister, and three companies in Guasave,

88
00:04:38,627 --> 00:04:41,367
a trucking firm, a service station,

89
00:04:41,387 --> 00:04:43,207
and a construction company.

90
00:04:44,527 --> 00:04:47,439
The charges, as listed by the FBI,

91
00:04:47,459 --> 00:04:49,533
were conspiracy to traffic cocaine,

92
00:04:49,553 --> 00:04:52,883
methamphetamine, heroin and marijuana into the United States,

93
00:04:52,903 --> 00:04:56,233
and the use and possession of a firearm.

94
00:04:57,553 --> 00:05:01,130
That same month, according to a report by CNN

95
00:05:01,150 --> 00:05:04,726
Mexico, he was seen with his family at a

96
00:05:04,746 --> 00:05:08,323
youth basketball game in a wealthy suburb of Monterrey.

97
00:05:08,343 --> 00:05:09,522
Nobody arrested him.

98
00:05:11,642 --> 00:05:13,811
And in February twenty twenty five,

99
00:05:13,831 --> 00:05:17,094
the FBI added him to its Ten Most Wanted

100
00:05:17,114 --> 00:05:20,378
list, with a reward of up to five million

101
00:05:20,398 --> 00:05:23,662
dollars. He was one of very few Mexican cartel

102
00:05:23,682 --> 00:05:25,851
figures ever placed on that list.

103
00:05:27,171 --> 00:05:30,498
We're following the cartel stories that matter right now.

104
00:05:30,518 --> 00:05:33,474
Subscribe, so you don't miss the next one.

105
00:05:35,614 --> 00:05:38,213
Chapter 4. The filing.

106
00:05:42,813 --> 00:05:44,871
This is where the story becomes strange.

107
00:05:46,991 --> 00:05:49,311
According to the Mexican outlet Infobae,

108
00:05:49,331 --> 00:05:52,821
citing a document first reported by the Tijuana weekly

109
00:05:52,841 --> 00:05:56,331
Zeta, a federal court in San Diego had a

110
00:05:56,351 --> 00:05:59,452
sealed indictment against him from April twenty nineteen.

111
00:06:00,772 --> 00:06:02,486
In May twenty twenty five,

112
00:06:02,506 --> 00:06:05,261
a prosecutor asked the court to unseal it.

113
00:06:05,281 --> 00:06:06,648
The filing, as reported,

114
00:06:06,668 --> 00:06:09,076
said that the defendant had been arrested,

115
00:06:09,096 --> 00:06:12,197
and had made his first appearance in court in

116
00:06:12,217 --> 00:06:12,891
San Diego.

117
00:06:14,211 --> 00:06:17,851
But he stayed on the FBI's Ten Most Wanted

118
00:06:17,871 --> 00:06:19,884
list. And eighteen months later,

119
00:06:19,904 --> 00:06:23,543
Mexican soldiers were fighting their way into Guasave to

120
00:06:23,563 --> 00:06:24,357
arrest him.

121
00:06:25,677 --> 00:06:29,050
The filing does not say when or where he

122
00:06:29,070 --> 00:06:31,313
was arrested, or what happened next.

123
00:06:31,333 --> 00:06:33,952
We have not seen the document ourselves.

124
00:06:33,972 --> 00:06:35,838
As of our latest check,

125
00:06:35,858 --> 00:06:39,231
neither the FBI nor the Justice Department has publicly

126
00:06:39,251 --> 00:06:39,986
explained it.

127
00:06:42,526 --> 00:06:45,787
Chapter 5. Operation Centella.

128
00:06:50,387 --> 00:06:52,377
According to Mexico's defense ministry,

129
00:06:52,397 --> 00:06:55,996
Mexico had been sharing surveillance information with the United

130
00:06:56,016 --> 00:06:58,006
States for about three months.

131
00:06:59,326 --> 00:07:01,402
A week before the operation,

132
00:07:01,422 --> 00:07:04,338
Mexico formally asked for American unmanned aircraft.

133
00:07:04,358 --> 00:07:08,111
It was the first time the ministry publicly confirmed

134
00:07:08,131 --> 00:07:09,789
the use of U.S.

135
00:07:09,809 --> 00:07:12,304
drones in an operation like this.

136
00:07:13,624 --> 00:07:16,554
On the evening of November twentieth,

137
00:07:16,574 --> 00:07:20,978
twenty twenty six, three hundred and sixty one Mexican

138
00:07:20,998 --> 00:07:24,419
personnel moved on a target in Guasave.

139
00:07:24,439 --> 00:07:27,369
Army special forces, National Guard units,

140
00:07:27,389 --> 00:07:28,844
paratroopers, and infantry.

141
00:07:30,164 --> 00:07:33,542
In the air, five armed Black Hawk helicopters,

142
00:07:33,562 --> 00:07:36,091
a Cougar helicopter, light attack aircraft,

143
00:07:36,111 --> 00:07:37,365
and a drone.

144
00:07:38,685 --> 00:07:41,008
According to the official account,

145
00:07:41,028 --> 00:07:44,758
the soldiers were attacked with firearms and explosives.

146
00:07:44,778 --> 00:07:47,101
The operation lasted for hours.

147
00:07:48,641 --> 00:07:52,366
Chapter 6. The night in Guasave.

148
00:07:56,966 --> 00:07:58,897
Four Mexican soldiers were killed.

149
00:08:01,417 --> 00:08:04,492
How many others died is disputed.

150
00:08:04,512 --> 00:08:08,618
Early reports spoke of eleven dead in total.

151
00:08:08,638 --> 00:08:10,682
Later, Mexico's security secretary,

152
00:08:10,702 --> 00:08:14,809
Omar García Harfuch, gave a figure of twenty.

153
00:08:14,829 --> 00:08:17,904
Sixteen alleged criminals, and four soldiers.

154
00:08:19,224 --> 00:08:21,344
Meza Flores was taken alive.

155
00:08:21,364 --> 00:08:25,195
Reports differ on how many people were arrested with

156
00:08:25,215 --> 00:08:28,191
him. Among them, according to Mexican media,

157
00:08:28,211 --> 00:08:32,043
was a man described as his second in command,

158
00:08:32,063 --> 00:08:34,183
and an alleged financial operator.

159
00:08:35,503 --> 00:08:39,937
Outside, his network reacted the way cartels in Sinaloa

160
00:08:39,957 --> 00:08:42,412
often do. According to reports,

161
00:08:42,432 --> 00:08:46,867
gunmen blocked roads across Guasave and nearby towns with

162
00:08:46,887 --> 00:08:48,847
burning trucks and cars.

163
00:08:48,867 --> 00:08:53,301
Sinaloa authorities counted ninety four vehicles used in the

164
00:08:53,321 --> 00:08:57,261
blockades. A baseball game had to be evacuated.

165
00:08:58,581 --> 00:09:01,269
In the early hours of November twenty first,

166
00:09:01,289 --> 00:09:02,962
according to the Associated Press,

167
00:09:02,982 --> 00:09:06,009
he was flown to Mexico City on a Mexican

168
00:09:06,029 --> 00:09:07,024
Air Force aircraft.

169
00:09:09,164 --> 00:09:12,913
Chapter 7. Not another Culiacanazo.

170
00:09:17,513 --> 00:09:20,326
In Mexico, the night brought back memories.

171
00:09:21,646 --> 00:09:23,603
In October twenty nineteen,

172
00:09:23,623 --> 00:09:25,581
soldiers captured Ovidio Guzmán,

173
00:09:25,601 --> 00:09:28,053
a son of El Chapo,

174
00:09:28,073 --> 00:09:32,502
in Culiacán. The cartel answered by taking over the

175
00:09:32,522 --> 00:09:34,974
city. The government released him.

176
00:09:34,994 --> 00:09:38,435
The day became known as the Culiacanazo.

177
00:09:39,755 --> 00:09:42,014
In January twenty twenty three,

178
00:09:42,034 --> 00:09:43,838
they captured Ovidio again.

179
00:09:43,858 --> 00:09:47,486
According to official figures reported at the time,

180
00:09:47,506 --> 00:09:49,309
twenty nine people died,

181
00:09:49,329 --> 00:09:52,501
including ten members of the security forces.

182
00:09:53,821 --> 00:09:56,845
This time, the government kept its prisoner.

183
00:09:56,865 --> 00:10:00,758
García Harfuch said the operation showed the strength of

184
00:10:00,778 --> 00:10:02,063
the Mexican state.

185
00:10:04,403 --> 00:10:07,013
Chapter 8. Washington.

186
00:10:11,613 --> 00:10:13,329
In the United States,

187
00:10:13,349 --> 00:10:15,065
the reaction was immediate.

188
00:10:15,085 --> 00:10:18,971
Donald Trump called the arrest a great success for

189
00:10:18,991 --> 00:10:20,273
Mexican security forces.

190
00:10:21,593 --> 00:10:25,165
FBI director Kash Patel said it was the eleventh

191
00:10:25,185 --> 00:10:28,756
capture of a Ten Most Wanted fugitive under the

192
00:10:28,776 --> 00:10:31,550
current administration. The head of the DEA,

193
00:10:31,570 --> 00:10:34,344
Terry Cole, called it a significant victory,

194
00:10:34,364 --> 00:10:37,137
and sent condolences for the four soldiers.

195
00:10:38,457 --> 00:10:40,811
The United States wants him.

196
00:10:40,831 --> 00:10:43,185
An extradition request is pending.

197
00:10:43,205 --> 00:10:45,085
But Mexico's attorney general,

198
00:10:45,105 --> 00:10:47,933
Ernestina Godoy, said that for now,

199
00:10:47,953 --> 00:10:51,257
he will be prosecuted in Mexico first.

200
00:10:52,577 --> 00:10:54,337
According to Mexican media,

201
00:10:54,357 --> 00:10:57,453
he was ordered held in pretrial detention,

202
00:10:57,473 --> 00:11:00,569
and was to be transferred to Altiplano,

203
00:11:00,589 --> 00:11:02,795
Mexico's maximum security federal prison.

204
00:11:02,815 --> 00:11:06,801
The same prison El Chapo Guzmán escaped from through

205
00:11:06,821 --> 00:11:09,027
a tunnel in twenty fifteen.

206
00:11:11,367 --> 00:11:14,036
Chapter 9. What comes next.

207
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:22,335
For Sinaloa, the arrest does not end the violence.

208
00:11:22,355 --> 00:11:23,988
Since twenty twenty four,

209
00:11:24,008 --> 00:11:27,707
factions of the Sinaloa Cartel have been fighting each

210
00:11:27,727 --> 00:11:29,774
other. According to local reports,

211
00:11:29,794 --> 00:11:33,493
thousands of people have been killed or have disappeared

212
00:11:33,513 --> 00:11:34,733
in the state.

213
00:11:36,053 --> 00:11:38,875
Removing one leader can open a vacuum.

214
00:11:38,895 --> 00:11:42,530
In Guasave, the question now is who fills it.

215
00:11:44,650 --> 00:11:46,293
For the United States,

216
00:11:46,313 --> 00:11:47,957
the question is simpler.

217
00:11:47,977 --> 00:11:51,701
When, and if, El Chapo Isidro will stand before

218
00:11:51,721 --> 00:11:55,445
an American judge. And whether that has already happened

219
00:11:55,465 --> 00:11:56,277
once before.

220
00:11:58,597 --> 00:12:00,827
Should Mexico send him north right away,

221
00:12:00,847 --> 00:12:02,757
or try him at home first?

222
00:12:02,777 --> 00:12:05,329
Tell us what you think in the comments.

223
00:12:08,149 --> 00:12:11,484
And to see how the first El Chapo escaped

